PART 3  does ANY orbit member satisfy a classical 3F2(1) theorem?
==============================================================================
rules applied to every one of the 7 orbit members, EXACTLY, for all x = 1/k:
  G  Gauss cancellation   (an upper equals a lower)     -> 2F1(1) = Gamma quotient
  R  contiguous reduction (upper - lower = m in Z_{>=1}) -> finite sum of 2F1(1)
  T  termination          (an upper in Z_{<=0})          -> + balanced = Saalschutz
  D  Dixon (well poised)      W  Watson       P  Whipple
  m up to 12; every solution is an EXACT rational x, admissible iff x = 1/k, k in Z_{>=1}

  k = 1 :
        D-Dixon              form [0]   well poised  (x = 1)
